// CR claude for claude: [bug/low] #partials is an unbounded 'a, so the check accepts a
// reference or a function, which the builtin can only refuse at run time ("a reference
// is not data", "partial values must be strings, got abstract:"). Bound it `'a: Data`
// here and in mod.gx, as data already is. probe:
// design/review-2026-10-26/repro/gx-stdlib-hbs-partials-unbounded.gx (gx-stdlib-05)
/// Render a Handlebars template with the given data context.
/// Use #partials to register named partial templates (as a struct or map).
/// Use #strict to error on missing variables instead of rendering empty strings.
val render: fn<'b: Data>(?#strict: bool, ?#partials: 'a, template: string, data: 'b) -> Result<string, `HbsErr(string)>;
